volume>172</volume><year>2006</year><fpage>185</fpage><lpage>188</lpage><ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://dx.doi.org/doi:10.1111/j.1469-8137.2006.01873.x">doi:10.1111/j.1469-8137.2006.01873.x</ext-link><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16995906</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1" position="float"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Internal and external mycelium of a vesicular arbuscular mycorrhizal fungus.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f01"/></fig><fig id="fig2" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Effects of the dimensionless parameter <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>. (<italic>a</italic>) Plot of equation <xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="fd2.11">(2.11)</xref> in dimensionless form. Analytical solution for the hyphal tip and length density in polar radial coordinates for different values of <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>. Solutions are shown at time <italic>t</italic>=3. (<italic>b</italic>) Overall hyphal length per unit root length for different values of the dimensionless parameter <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>, computed in equation <xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="fd2.13">(2.13)</xref>. (<italic>a</italic>,<italic>b</italic>) Solid line, <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>=0.01; dashed line, <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>=1; dot-dashed line, <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>=10.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f02"/></fig><fig id="fig3" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Model including nonlinear branching, tip&#x02013;tip anastomosis and the effect of varying <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>1</sub> (solid line, <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>1</sub>=0; dashed line, <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>1</sub>=1; dot-dashed line, <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>1</sub>=10). Solutions are shown at time <italic>t</italic>=3. Values of other dimensionless parameters are as follows: <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>=1 and <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>2</sub>=0. The following are the numerical solution parameters: <italic>J</italic>=300, <italic>&#x003bc;</italic>=0.8 and &#x00394;<italic>t</italic>=0.01, where <italic>J</italic> is the number of spatial grid points; <inline-formula><inline-graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250e02.jpg" alternate-form-of="M2"/><mml:math id="M2"><mml:mrow><mml:mi>&#x003bc;</mml:mi><mml:mo>=</mml:mo><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">&#x00394;</mml:mi><mml:mi>t</mml:mi><mml:mo>/</mml:mo><mml:mi mathvariant="normal">&#x00394;</mml:mi><mml:mi>r</mml:mi></mml:mrow></mml:math></inline-formula>; &#x00394;<italic>t</italic> is the time-step size; and &#x00394;<italic>r</italic> is the spatial step size.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f03"/></fig><fig id="fig4" position="float"><label>Figure 4</label><caption><p>Model including tip&#x02013;hypha anastomosis and the effect of varying <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>2</sub> (solid line, <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>2</sub>=0; dashed line, <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>2</sub>=1; dot-dashed line, <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>2</sub>=10). Solutions are shown at time <italic>t</italic>=3. Values of other dimensionless parameters are as follows: <italic>&#x003b4;</italic>=1 and <italic>&#x003b1;</italic><sub>1</sub>=0. Numerical solution parameters are the same as given in figure 3 legend.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f04"/></fig><fig id="fig5" position="float"><label>Figure 5</label><caption><p>Plot of the linear model given by equation <xref ref-type="disp-formula" rid="fd2.10">(2.10)</xref> in comparison with data for <italic>S. calospora</italic>. See <xref ref-type="table" rid="tbl1">table 1</xref> for corresponding model parameter values. Hyphal length densities at (<italic>a</italic>) 0 days, (<italic>b</italic>) 7 days, (<italic>c</italic>) 14 days, (<italic>d</italic>) 28 days and (<italic>e</italic>) 47 days.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f05"/></fig><fig id="fig6" position="float"><label>Figure 6</label><caption><p>Plot of the general model in comparison with data for <italic>Glomus</italic> sp. See <xref ref-type="table" rid="tbl1">table 1</xref> for corresponding model parameter values. Numerical solution parameters are the same as given in figure 3 legend. Hyphal length densities at (<italic>a</italic>) 0 days, (<italic>b</italic>) 7 days, (<italic>c</italic>) 14 days, (<italic>d</italic>) 28 days and (<italic>e</italic>) 47 days.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f06"/></fig><fig id="fig7" position="float"><label>Figure 7</label><caption><p>Plot of the general model in comparison with data for <italic>A. laevis</italic>. See <xref ref-type="table" rid="tbl1">table 1</xref> for corresponding model parameter values. Numerical solution parameters are the same as given in figure 3 legend. Hyphal length densities at (<italic>a</italic>) 0 days, (<italic>b</italic>) 7 days, (<italic>c</italic>) 14 days, (<italic>d</italic>) 28 days and (<italic>e</italic>) 47 days.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="rsif20071250f07"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p>Fitted parameter values for the three fungal species considered.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th valign="bottom" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">parameter</th><th valign="bottom" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">notation</th><th valign="bottom" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">units</th><th valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>S. calospora</italic></th><th valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>Glomus</italic> sp.</th><th valign="bottom" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>A. laevis</italic></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">speed of tip movement</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>v</italic></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">cm d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.25</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.13</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.28</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">tip branching rate</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>b</italic><sub><italic>n</italic></sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.02</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.91</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.47</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">tip death rate</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>d</italic><sub><italic>n</italic></sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">5.20&#x000d7;10<sup>&#x02212;3</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.15</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.73</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">net tip branching rate</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>b</italic>=<italic>b</italic><sub><italic>n</italic></sub>&#x02212;<italic>d</italic><sub><italic>n</italic></sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.015</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.76</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.74</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">hyphal death rate</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>d</italic></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.18</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.28</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.08</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">maximal hyphal tip density</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>n</italic><sub>max</sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">cm<sup>&#x02212;3</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">2238.14</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.78&#x000d7;10<sup>5</sup></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">tip&#x02013;tip anastomosis rate</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>a</italic><sub>1</sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">cm<sup>3</sup>&#x0200a;d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">7.00&#x000d7;10<sup>&#x02212;7</sup></td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">tip&#x02013;hypha anastomosis rate</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>a</italic><sub>2</sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">cm<sup>3</sup>&#x0200a;m<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>&#x0200a;d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02014;</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.15</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">boundary proliferation</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>a</italic></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">m cm<sup>&#x02212;3</sup>&#x0200a;d<sup>&#x02212;1</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.52</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">2.24</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.56</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">initial tip density at boundary</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>n</italic><sub>0,<italic>b</italic></sub></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">cm<sup>&#x02212;3</sup></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">97.07</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">84.16</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">12.68</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">RMSE</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.11</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.67<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn1">a</xref> 2.38<xref ref-type="table-fn" rid="tblfn2">b</xref></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">1.33</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tblfn1"><label>a</label><p>Not including the data point at 1&#x0200a;cm distance after 14 days.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot><table-wrap-foot><fn id="tblfn2"><label>b</label><p>Including the data point at 1&#x0200a;cm distance after 14 days.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>